1
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:04,540
You're here.

2
00:00:05,760 --> 00:00:07,380
Your organs are failing.

3
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:09,300
And your death is drawing near.

4
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:13,440
But if you bribe the right politicians in the right order at the right time,

5
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:16,600
you can trade the nuclear warheads for medicine.

6
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:20,080
And it's not even a crime.

7
00:01:39,984 --> 00:01:46,324
Genetic Slavery Your government spends six hundred and four more on weapons

8
00:01:46,324 --> 00:01:47,644
than on curing disease,

9
00:01:48,264 --> 00:01:49,824
and you think that's a political problem.

10
00:01:50,404 --> 00:01:50,904
It's not.

11
00:01:51,304 --> 00:01:52,584
It's a hardware problem.

12
00:01:53,204 --> 00:01:57,524
You're running two hundred thousand year old software optimized for hoarding

13
00:01:57,524 --> 00:02:01,724
rocks and fearing strangers, and you've given it nuclear weapons.

14
00:02:02,304 --> 00:02:06,824
This chapter is the owner's manual for the brain that's trying to kill you.

15
00:02:07,024 --> 00:02:12,624
How Hydrogen Learned to Worry (A thirteen point eight billion year recap).

16
00:02:12,624 --> 00:02:17,324
Thirteen point eight billion years ago, the universe exploded.

17
00:02:17,884 --> 00:02:22,064
This was the last time anything interesting happened for about four hundred

18
00:02:22,064 --> 00:02:23,024
million years.

19
00:02:23,584 --> 00:02:28,164
Then hydrogen atoms, which had been drifting around doing nothing (hydrogen

20
00:02:28,164 --> 00:02:32,214
is the simplest element because the universe started with low expectations),

21
00:02:32,214 --> 00:02:37,104
began clumping together until they got so dense they caught fire.

22
00:02:37,104 --> 00:02:39,904
These fires are called "stars."

23
00:02:41,024 --> 00:02:43,924
Stars are the universe's first manufacturing process:

24
00:02:44,484 --> 00:02:48,684
they take hydrogen, crush it into heavier elements like carbon and oxygen,

25
00:02:49,064 --> 00:02:50,284
and then explode,

26
00:02:51,104 --> 00:02:52,784
scattering their products across space.

27
00:02:53,364 --> 00:02:56,764
The workplace fatality rate is one hundred percent.

28
00:02:56,764 --> 00:03:00,424
This went on for about nine billion years.

29
00:03:01,044 --> 00:03:07,684
Then, on one unremarkable rock orbiting one unremarkable star in one unremarkable

30
00:03:07,684 --> 00:03:09,784
galaxy (the one you named "dirt"),

31
00:03:10,804 --> 00:03:13,204
carbon atoms started doing something unusual.

32
00:03:14,064 --> 00:03:17,444
Carbon is the most promiscuous element in the periodic table;

33
00:03:17,804 --> 00:03:19,784
it will bond with almost anything.

34
00:03:20,484 --> 00:03:25,704
On your particular rock, it bonded with hydrogen, oxygen, and nitrogen in

35
00:03:25,704 --> 00:03:29,264
arrangements that could do one very specific trick:

36
00:03:30,064 --> 00:03:30,884
copy themselves.

37
00:03:31,704 --> 00:03:34,804
This was the moment everything went wrong.

38
00:03:35,464 --> 00:03:38,764
The molecules that were better at copying made more copies.

39
00:03:39,224 --> 00:03:41,764
The ones that were worse at copying made fewer.

40
00:03:42,264 --> 00:03:45,944
This is the entire plot of the next four billion years.

41
00:03:46,204 --> 00:03:51,564
It is also the entire plot of your economy, your politics, your wars, and

42
00:03:51,564 --> 00:03:53,904
your inability to fund clinical trials.

43
00:03:53,904 --> 00:03:56,084
Everything else is a footnote.

44
00:03:57,264 --> 00:03:58,124
Including you.

45
00:03:59,344 --> 00:04:04,664
Four billion years of copying molecules competing with other copying molecules

46
00:04:04,664 --> 00:04:09,664
eventually produced a copying molecule so complicated it could look up at

47
00:04:09,664 --> 00:04:11,444
the stars that made it and ask,

48
00:04:12,104 --> 00:04:14,404
"Why am I anxious about a meeting tomorrow?"

49
00:04:15,064 --> 00:04:15,964
The answer is:

50
00:04:15,964 --> 00:04:21,704
because anxiety made your ancestors copy more effectively than calm did.

51
00:04:21,704 --> 00:04:27,784
You are a temporary vehicle that copying molecules built to make more copying

52
00:04:27,784 --> 00:04:32,444
molecules, and the vehicle has become sentient enough to realize this, which

53
00:04:32,444 --> 00:04:36,184
is either the most beautiful or the most horrifying thing in the universe

54
00:04:36,704 --> 00:04:40,044
depending on how you feel about being a meat taxi for chemistry.

55
00:04:41,144 --> 00:04:43,444
But the vehicle wasn't built all at once.

56
00:04:43,684 --> 00:04:48,884
It was built in layers, like a bad renovation where nobody removed the previous

57
00:04:48,884 --> 00:04:49,704
tenants' plumbing.

58
00:04:49,704 --> 00:04:52,404
First came the reptilian brain:

59
00:04:52,864 --> 00:04:57,364
the oldest layer, roughly five hundred million years old, handling the functions

60
00:04:57,364 --> 00:04:59,924
so basic they're barely worth listing

61
00:05:00,524 --> 00:05:01,484
(breathe, eat,

62
00:05:02,104 --> 00:05:05,944
fight, flee, reproduce, regulate body temperature).

63
00:05:06,684 --> 00:05:08,664
This is the brain you share with lizards.

64
00:05:09,144 --> 00:05:10,344
It has no feelings.

65
00:05:10,664 --> 00:05:12,044
It has no opinions.

66
00:05:12,044 --> 00:05:17,984
It has reflexes, and those reflexes kept vertebrates alive for three hundred

67
00:05:17,984 --> 00:05:21,044
million years before anything with fur showed up.

68
00:05:21,464 --> 00:05:22,204
It's still running.

69
00:05:22,684 --> 00:05:23,904
It's running right now.

70
00:05:24,364 --> 00:05:27,304
It's the reason your heart is beating without your permission.

71
00:05:27,744 --> 00:05:31,504
Then, about two hundred million years ago, mammals evolved the limbic system

72
00:05:31,504 --> 00:05:35,644
on top of the reptile brain, like building a nursery on top of a weapons

73
00:05:35,644 --> 00:05:36,144
depot.

74
00:05:36,584 --> 00:05:38,404
This is your emotional brain.

75
00:05:38,684 --> 00:05:42,444
It's the reason you bond with your children instead of eating them (a genuine

76
00:05:42,444 --> 00:05:44,124
upgrade over the reptilian model).

77
00:05:44,704 --> 00:05:48,124
It handles fear, pleasure, memory, and social bonding.

78
00:05:48,584 --> 00:05:52,444
It's the reason you cry at movies, love your dog, and feel a physical ache

79
00:05:52,444 --> 00:05:54,064
when someone you care about is hurting.

80
00:05:54,324 --> 00:05:58,383
It is also the reason you make catastrophically stupid decisions when you're

81
00:05:58,383 --> 00:06:03,064
angry, aroused, or afraid, because the limbic system processes information

82
00:06:03,064 --> 00:06:07,064
faster than the part of your brain that thinks, and by the time thinking

83
00:06:07,064 --> 00:06:11,064
arrives, the limbic system has already committed you to a course of action

84
00:06:11,484 --> 00:06:13,364
you'll spend the next decade regretting.

85
00:06:13,644 --> 00:06:18,244
Finally, very recently in evolutionary terms (roughly two to three million

86
00:06:18,244 --> 00:06:22,924
years ago, which is yesterday by the universe's standards), the neocortex

87
00:06:22,924 --> 00:06:24,164
expanded dramatically.

88
00:06:24,884 --> 00:06:27,284
This is the part you think of as "you."

89
00:06:27,624 --> 00:06:32,544
It handles language, abstract reasoning, planning, and the ability to contemplate

90
00:06:32,544 --> 00:06:36,104
your own mortality and then do absolutely nothing about it.

91
00:06:36,104 --> 00:06:41,044
It's the thinnest layer, the newest addition, and the most easily overridden.

92
00:06:41,244 --> 00:06:45,844
Your neocortex can calculate orbital mechanics, prove mathematical theorems,

93
00:06:45,924 --> 00:06:47,624
and design nuclear reactors.

94
00:06:48,224 --> 00:06:52,384
Your limbic system can shut all of that down with a single flush of cortisol

95
00:06:52,384 --> 00:06:54,144
because someone looked at you funny.

96
00:06:54,684 --> 00:06:58,804
Your reptilian brain can override both of them simultaneously because it

97
00:06:58,804 --> 00:06:59,904
heard a loud noise.

98
00:07:00,144 --> 00:07:03,944
You are three brains in a trench coat pretending to be one person.

99
00:07:03,944 --> 00:07:05,964
The reptile wants to survive.

100
00:07:06,524 --> 00:07:07,904
The mammal wants to be loved.

101
00:07:08,424 --> 00:07:10,404
The human wants to understand the universe.

102
00:07:11,064 --> 00:07:15,264
They take turns driving, none of them have a license, and the reptile has

103
00:07:15,264 --> 00:07:15,864
seniority.

104
00:07:16,084 --> 00:07:17,684
The chemicals don't know you exist.

105
00:07:18,024 --> 00:07:19,004
They have no plan.

106
00:07:19,244 --> 00:07:20,104
They can't plan.

107
00:07:20,404 --> 00:07:21,004
They're chemicals.

108
00:07:21,684 --> 00:07:26,464
But through thirteen point eight billion years of mindless repetition, they

109
00:07:26,464 --> 00:07:30,884
produced a species with three stacked brains that can split atoms, write

110
00:07:30,884 --> 00:07:35,584
symphonies, and cure diseases, but mostly uses these abilities to argue

111
00:07:35,584 --> 00:07:37,244
on the internet and build weapons.

112
00:07:37,784 --> 00:07:40,144
If you're looking for someone to blame, there's nobody.

113
00:07:40,664 --> 00:07:45,404
There's just hydrogen, which caught fire and then got very, very out of hand.

114
00:07:45,404 --> 00:07:49,224
The Selfish Gene Made You Illogical (It Was a Good Idea at the Time).

115
00:07:49,684 --> 00:07:54,024
For about a century, your biologists were stuck on a puzzle that, from the

116
00:07:54,024 --> 00:07:56,284
outside, was hilarious to watch.

117
00:07:56,284 --> 00:07:59,784
Darwin said natural selection acts on individuals:

118
00:08:00,364 --> 00:08:03,564
the fittest survive, the weakest don't, end of story.

119
00:08:04,344 --> 00:08:09,324
Elegant, simple, and completely unable to explain why a ground squirrel

120
00:08:09,324 --> 00:08:13,864
would scream to warn its colony about a hawk, thereby making itself the

121
00:08:13,864 --> 00:08:15,084
most obvious target.

122
00:08:15,704 --> 00:08:19,304
Individual selection says that squirrel should shut up and let everyone

123
00:08:19,304 --> 00:08:20,024
else get eaten.

124
00:08:20,484 --> 00:08:21,464
The screamer dies.

125
00:08:21,804 --> 00:08:23,044
The quiet ones survive.

126
00:08:23,664 --> 00:08:26,684
Within a few generations, screaming should be extinct.

127
00:08:27,184 --> 00:08:27,884
But it isn't.

128
00:08:28,224 --> 00:08:29,784
The squirrels keep screaming.

129
00:08:30,564 --> 00:08:35,164
Darwin's theory, applied to individuals, predicts a world of pure selfishness.

130
00:08:35,584 --> 00:08:39,904
Your world has firefighters, organ donors, and people who jump on grenades.

131
00:08:40,664 --> 00:08:42,124
Something didn't add up.

132
00:08:42,724 --> 00:08:45,604
So some of your biologists tried group selection:

133
00:08:45,964 --> 00:08:48,444
maybe evolution acts on whole groups.

134
00:08:49,164 --> 00:08:52,764
Altruistic groups outcompete selfish groups, so altruism survives.

135
00:08:53,344 --> 00:08:56,824
This sounded lovely and was almost entirely wrong.

136
00:08:57,384 --> 00:08:58,864
The problem is cheaters.

137
00:08:59,324 --> 00:09:03,884
Drop one selfish individual into an altruistic group, and that individual

138
00:09:03,884 --> 00:09:08,504
gets all the benefits of everyone else's sacrifice while paying none of

139
00:09:08,504 --> 00:09:09,024
the costs.

140
00:09:09,504 --> 00:09:11,204
The selfish gene spreads.

141
00:09:11,724 --> 00:09:13,424
The altruistic ones disappear.

142
00:09:13,424 --> 00:09:17,484
Within a few generations, the group is full of cheaters again.

143
00:09:18,304 --> 00:09:21,484
Group selection is the evolutionary equivalent of communism:

144
00:09:22,184 --> 00:09:23,164
beautiful on paper,

145
00:09:23,784 --> 00:09:27,344
immediately destroyed by the first person who realizes they can get away

146
00:09:27,344 --> 00:09:28,424
with not contributing.

147
00:09:29,184 --> 00:09:32,524
Your biologists spent decades arguing about this.

148
00:09:32,904 --> 00:09:37,264
On Wishonia, we found the debate very entertaining, in the way you find

149
00:09:37,264 --> 00:09:40,724
it entertaining when someone can't find the glasses they're already wearing.

150
00:09:40,724 --> 00:09:45,764
The answer, when it finally arrived, was so simple it was almost insulting.

151
00:09:46,484 --> 00:09:50,844
Hamilton and then Dawkins pointed out that neither the individual nor the

152
00:09:50,844 --> 00:09:52,524
group is the unit of selection.

153
00:09:53,144 --> 00:09:54,284
The gene is.

154
00:09:54,904 --> 00:09:58,004
Genes don't care about the organism they're sitting in.

155
00:09:58,284 --> 00:10:02,744
They care about copies of themselves, wherever those copies happen to be.

156
00:10:03,164 --> 00:10:07,004
That screaming ground squirrel isn't sacrificing itself for the group.

157
00:10:07,324 --> 00:10:11,544
It's sacrificing itself for its relatives, who carry copies of the same

158
00:10:11,544 --> 00:10:14,244
genes, including the gene for screaming.

159
00:10:14,884 --> 00:10:15,984
The math works:

160
00:10:16,424 --> 00:10:20,704
if the scream saves enough copies of the screaming gene in nearby relatives,

161
00:10:21,143 --> 00:10:22,163
the gene spreads,

162
00:10:22,824 --> 00:10:25,444
even though the individual screamer gets eaten.

163
00:10:25,984 --> 00:10:27,664
The organism is disposable.

164
00:10:28,284 --> 00:10:29,844
The gene is what matters.

165
00:10:30,504 --> 00:10:32,564
You are not the main character.

166
00:10:33,024 --> 00:10:34,524
You are the packaging.

167
00:10:34,524 --> 00:10:36,944
Richard Dawkins put it perfectly:

168
00:10:37,684 --> 00:10:42,564
"We are survival machines, robot vehicles blindly programmed to preserve

169
00:10:42,564 --> 00:10:45,244
the selfish molecules known as genes."

170
00:10:45,244 --> 00:10:45,924
Translation:

171
00:10:45,924 --> 00:10:50,044
You're a meat puppet controlled by chemicals whose entire business plan

172
00:10:50,044 --> 00:10:53,084
is "make more chemicals before something eats us."

173
00:10:53,464 --> 00:10:57,384
On Wishonia, when we first intercepted this description, we thought it was

174
00:10:57,384 --> 00:10:57,884
satire.

175
00:10:58,304 --> 00:11:02,364
Then we observed your behavior and realized it was the most accurate description

176
00:11:02,364 --> 00:11:07,604
of a sentient species anyone had ever written, which is sad, but also very

177
00:11:07,604 --> 00:11:10,704
useful, because accurate descriptions are how you fix things.

178
00:11:11,444 --> 00:11:13,404
Your genes don't care if you're happy.

179
00:11:13,664 --> 00:11:15,884
They don't care if you live past thirty.

180
00:11:15,884 --> 00:11:17,864
They care about exactly one thing:

181
00:11:18,284 --> 00:11:21,724
making copies of themselves before something with teeth finds you.

182
00:11:22,184 --> 00:11:27,104
This is the entire explanation for human behavior, and every other explanation

183
00:11:27,104 --> 00:11:28,044
is a footnote.

184
00:11:28,804 --> 00:11:31,164
The mechanism is elegant in its cruelty.

185
00:11:31,164 --> 00:11:33,744
Your genes have exactly two tools:

186
00:11:34,404 --> 00:11:35,324
pleasure and pain.

187
00:11:36,024 --> 00:11:36,864
Pleasure is the carrot:

188
00:11:37,264 --> 00:11:40,604
eat sugar, feel good, gain calories, survive winter.

189
00:11:41,224 --> 00:11:46,044
Engage in regrettable intercourse, feel good, make copies, mission accomplished.

190
00:11:46,744 --> 00:11:47,844
Pain is the stick:

191
00:11:48,404 --> 00:11:53,864
touch fire, feel agony, never touch fire again, keep the meat vehicle intact.

192
00:11:54,644 --> 00:11:59,024
Every decision you think you're making freely is actually your genes yanking

193
00:11:59,024 --> 00:12:03,224
these two levers like a puppet master who took one management course and

194
00:12:03,224 --> 00:12:06,744
learned that rewards and punishments are the only two things that work.

195
00:12:07,364 --> 00:12:12,524
Your entire moral philosophy, your deepest loves, your most transcendent

196
00:12:12,524 --> 00:12:13,864
spiritual experiences:

197
00:12:14,444 --> 00:12:19,044
all of it is chemicals bribing and threatening a nervous system into doing

198
00:12:19,044 --> 00:12:20,564
what's good for the molecules.

199
00:12:21,104 --> 00:12:26,744
On Wishonia, we find this simultaneously the most elegant and the most disturbing

200
00:12:26,744 --> 00:12:28,584
engineering we've ever observed.

201
00:12:29,364 --> 00:12:34,004
For ninety-nine point nine percent of human history, this was brilliant

202
00:12:34,004 --> 00:12:34,704
engineering.

203
00:12:35,144 --> 00:12:38,884
The tribes that were paranoid, violent, and territorial survived.

204
00:12:39,484 --> 00:12:43,824
The ones that were trusting, peaceful, and generous were eaten by the paranoid

205
00:12:43,824 --> 00:12:48,244
ones, which is evolution's way of saying "nice guys finish extinct."

206
00:12:49,024 --> 00:12:53,584
Now your paranoia makes you distrust strangers you need to cooperate with.

207
00:12:53,584 --> 00:12:57,444
Your territorial instincts make you build weapons you'll never use.

208
00:12:57,864 --> 00:13:01,764
Your tribal loyalty makes you fight over territory you don't need.

209
00:13:02,304 --> 00:13:03,844
The genes are still celebrating.

210
00:13:04,384 --> 00:13:05,464
You are not.

211
00:13:06,444 --> 00:13:07,344
Part one:

212
00:13:07,344 --> 00:13:10,764
Your Brain Was Optimized for a World That Doesn't Exist.

213
00:13:11,524 --> 00:13:13,384
The Violence Module (Or:

214
00:13:13,384 --> 00:13:16,964
Why You Tend to Prefer Bombs Over Clinical Trials).

215
00:13:16,964 --> 00:13:21,424
Fifteen to thirty percent of your ancestors died from violence.

216
00:13:21,424 --> 00:13:22,564
Not disease.

217
00:13:23,044 --> 00:13:23,604
Not starvation.

218
00:13:24,444 --> 00:13:28,504
Other humans, smashing their heads with rocks over territorial disputes

219
00:13:28,504 --> 00:13:29,924
about berry bushes.

220
00:13:30,844 --> 00:13:34,904
You've since upgraded the rocks to intercontinental ballistic missiles,

221
00:13:35,264 --> 00:13:37,224
but the berry bush energy remains.

222
00:13:38,464 --> 00:13:42,044
This is what biologists call "conserved behavior."

223
00:13:42,644 --> 00:13:47,064
It means the behavior has been preserved across millions of years because

224
00:13:47,064 --> 00:13:50,444
it was so useful that evolution never bothered to remove it.

225
00:13:50,924 --> 00:13:54,744
On your planet, it's the reason you spend more preparing to kill each other

226
00:13:54,744 --> 00:13:56,524
than preparing to not die.

227
00:13:57,524 --> 00:14:00,844
The behavior was designed for a world where the stranger approaching your

228
00:14:00,844 --> 00:14:02,524
camp might eat your children.

229
00:14:02,944 --> 00:14:04,584
In that world, it was rational.

230
00:14:05,024 --> 00:14:10,304
In a world with nuclear weapons, it's the reason I'm writing this manual. The tribes that survived assumed every stranger might want to kill them (often statistically accurate), struck first when threatened (natural selection at work), formed tight combat groups to kill other groups (teamwork!), and hoarded weapons obsessively (can never have too many pointy sticks). Your brain is still running this exact software. That's why you instinctively distrust people who don't look like your tribe, why Twitter arguments feel like actual combat (your amygdala genuinely can't tell the difference), and why countries with thousands of nuclear weapons are worried they don't have enough. The violence module kept your ancestors from getting clubbed to death. Now it's building weapons that could end all life on Earth. Computer scientists call this "feature creep." Biologists call it "maladaptive." I call it "the most expensive software bug in the history of any civilization I've observed, and I've observed eight hundred and forty-seven.".

231
00:14:10,304 --> 00:14:11,804
The Tribal Brain (Or:

232
00:14:11,804 --> 00:14:14,724
Why Democracy Was Always Going to Be a Mess).

233
00:14:16,024 --> 00:14:20,584
Dunbar's number says humans can maintain stable relationships with about

234
00:14:20,584 --> 00:14:22,504
one hundred and fifty people.

235
00:14:22,984 --> 00:14:25,024
That's your entire social capacity.

236
00:14:25,664 --> 00:14:30,004
Your brain has one hundred and fifty slots for caring about people, and

237
00:14:30,004 --> 00:14:34,244
you've filled most of them with coworkers you tolerate and celebrities who

238
00:14:34,244 --> 00:14:35,224
don't know you exist.

239
00:14:36,044 --> 00:14:40,664
Your brain treats anything outside your one hundred and fifty person monkeysphere

240
00:14:40,664 --> 00:14:41,804
as an abstraction.

241
00:14:41,804 --> 00:14:47,124
You care more about your neighbor's barking dog than ten thousand people

242
00:14:47,124 --> 00:14:52,204
dying of malaria, because the dog is RIGHT THERE being loud and malaria

243
00:14:52,204 --> 00:14:54,864
is just a concept with numbers attached.

244
00:14:56,044 --> 00:14:59,864
Local corruption makes you angrier than trillion dollar Pentagon waste,

245
00:15:00,224 --> 00:15:04,184
because the local guy stole ten thousand dollars you can imagine, while

246
00:15:04,304 --> 00:15:05,444
according to D.O.D.

247
00:15:05,444 --> 00:15:10,264
audit failures the Pentagon lost two point five trillion dollars, which

248
00:15:10,264 --> 00:15:11,484
is just syllables.

249
00:15:12,584 --> 00:15:17,544
You'll donate to save one sick child whose face you can see but ignore statistics

250
00:15:17,544 --> 00:15:22,844
about millions, because one child has eyes and millions is just a very big

251
00:15:22,844 --> 00:15:25,804
number that makes your brain hurt and then change the channel.

252
00:15:26,604 --> 00:15:30,284
Democracy asks this brain to make civilization-level decisions.

253
00:15:30,284 --> 00:15:35,004
It goes exactly as well as asking a labrador retriever to do your taxes.

254
00:15:35,704 --> 00:15:39,004
You vote based on who looks stronger, because your brain thinks the election

255
00:15:39,004 --> 00:15:40,084
is a wrestling match.

256
00:15:40,664 --> 00:15:44,324
You vote based on who your tribe likes, because if the clan approves, must

257
00:15:44,324 --> 00:15:44,824
be good.

258
00:15:45,384 --> 00:15:49,184
You vote based on who makes you feel safe, because fear sells better than

259
00:15:49,184 --> 00:15:50,344
policy ever will.

260
00:15:50,804 --> 00:15:54,444
And you vote based on who you'd have a beer with, which has zero relevance

261
00:15:54,444 --> 00:15:55,524
to nuclear policy.

262
00:15:55,524 --> 00:16:00,164
You elect leaders using the same brain circuits your ancestors used to pick

263
00:16:00,164 --> 00:16:01,364
the guy with the biggest club.

264
00:16:01,924 --> 00:16:05,684
The guy with the biggest club is now in charge of the biggest nuclear arsenal,

265
00:16:06,124 --> 00:16:09,464
and your brain sees no problem with this, because your brain was designed

266
00:16:09,464 --> 00:16:11,704
before clubs could destroy continents.

267
00:16:12,984 --> 00:16:14,824
The Compassion Gradient (Or:

268
00:16:14,824 --> 00:16:18,504
Why You'll Buy Your Cat a Birthday Cake While Children Starve).

269
00:16:19,744 --> 00:16:24,224
Hamilton's Rule is the most important equation your species has never heard of.

270
00:16:24,224 --> 00:16:25,064
It says:

271
00:16:25,704 --> 00:16:30,284
help someone if the benefit to them, multiplied by your genetic relatedness,

272
00:16:30,284 --> 00:16:32,224
exceeds the cost to you.

273
00:16:32,724 --> 00:16:33,264
In math:

274
00:16:33,264 --> 00:16:35,284
r B is greater than C.

275
00:16:35,904 --> 00:16:38,024
Your genes don't do universal compassion.

276
00:16:38,544 --> 00:16:41,584
They do a cost-benefit analysis based on shared D.N.A.

277
00:16:42,084 --> 00:16:45,844
They've been doing it for four billion years, and they are very, very good

278
00:16:45,844 --> 00:16:46,344
at it.

279
00:16:46,804 --> 00:16:50,744
The result is a compassion gradient so precise it could be graphed.

280
00:16:50,744 --> 00:16:54,004
You'd die for your children, who share fifty percent of your genes.

281
00:16:54,604 --> 00:16:56,144
You'd probably die for your siblings,

282
00:16:56,764 --> 00:16:57,784
depending on which sibling.

283
00:16:58,424 --> 00:17:00,644
You'd lend money to your cousins, reluctantly.

284
00:17:01,424 --> 00:17:02,364
You'd fight for your tribe.

285
00:17:02,824 --> 00:17:04,364
You'd wave a flag for your nation.

286
00:17:04,964 --> 00:17:07,844
You'd change the channel to avoid thinking about strangers.

287
00:17:08,544 --> 00:17:09,204
And other species?

288
00:17:09,844 --> 00:17:10,584
You'd eat them.

289
00:17:11,064 --> 00:17:15,324
The gradient runs from infinite compassion for yourself to zero for anything

290
00:17:15,324 --> 00:17:16,804
that doesn't share your D.N.A.

291
00:17:17,344 --> 00:17:18,404
It's not a metaphor.

292
00:17:18,724 --> 00:17:19,444
It's a budget.

293
00:17:20,044 --> 00:17:25,544
This is the literal mechanism behind racism, speciesism, and every form

294
00:17:25,544 --> 00:17:28,344
of in-group preference your species has ever invented.

295
00:17:28,924 --> 00:17:31,984
Your genes designed you to favor people who look like you.

296
00:17:32,324 --> 00:17:35,324
For two hundred thousand years, people who looked like you were probably

297
00:17:35,324 --> 00:17:39,164
related to you, and helping them helped your shared genes copy themselves.

298
00:17:39,844 --> 00:17:41,444
So racism isn't a malfunction.

299
00:17:41,944 --> 00:17:44,884
It's the system working exactly as designed.

300
00:17:44,884 --> 00:17:49,124
That's considerably worse than a malfunction, because malfunctions can be

301
00:17:49,124 --> 00:17:50,324
fixed with a software patch.

302
00:17:50,904 --> 00:17:52,664
This is the software.

303
00:17:53,084 --> 00:17:57,484
It also explains the single most irrational resource allocation decision

304
00:17:57,484 --> 00:18:01,304
your species makes every year, which is impressive given the competition.

305
00:18:01,884 --> 00:18:05,564
You will spend fifty dollars on a birthday present your cousin doesn't want,

306
00:18:05,964 --> 00:18:09,914
won't use, and will re-gift to someone who also won't use it, while five

307
00:18:09,914 --> 00:18:13,764
dollars worth of mosquito bed nets would prevent a child's death from malaria

308
00:18:13,764 --> 00:18:15,124
in sub-Saharan Africa.

309
00:18:15,784 --> 00:18:19,724
Your genes would rather waste ten times the resources on a relative than

310
00:18:19,724 --> 00:18:20,664
save a stranger.

311
00:18:21,164 --> 00:18:24,044
By any rational calculation, this is insane.

312
00:18:24,544 --> 00:18:26,784
By Hamilton's Rule, it's exactly correct.

313
00:18:27,364 --> 00:18:29,784
The child in Africa is genetically a stranger.

314
00:18:30,204 --> 00:18:31,304
Your cousin is not.

315
00:18:31,764 --> 00:18:32,564
The math is clear:

316
00:18:33,004 --> 00:18:35,344
let the stranger die, buy the cousin a candle.

317
00:18:36,184 --> 00:18:40,264
On Wishonia, when we first modeled this behavior, we assumed our simulation

318
00:18:40,264 --> 00:18:41,004
was broken.

319
00:18:41,004 --> 00:18:43,784
We re-ran it three hundred and forty times.

320
00:18:44,164 --> 00:18:45,484
The simulation was fine.

321
00:18:45,864 --> 00:18:47,884
Your species is actually like this.

322
00:18:48,504 --> 00:18:52,913
You have pet supply stores that sell Halloween costumes for dogs while seven

323
00:18:52,913 --> 00:18:55,504
hundred million humans lack clean water.

324
00:18:55,964 --> 00:18:59,404
You spend more on birthday cards for people you're obligated to pretend

325
00:18:59,404 --> 00:19:02,803
to like than on preventing the deaths of people you've never met.

326
00:19:03,484 --> 00:19:04,924
And here's the part that should alarm you:

327
00:19:05,323 --> 00:19:07,184
this feels completely normal.

328
00:19:07,684 --> 00:19:09,644
It doesn't feel like a moral catastrophe.

329
00:19:09,644 --> 00:19:10,864
It feels like Tuesday.

330
00:19:11,604 --> 00:19:13,264
That's the gradient working.

331
00:19:13,884 --> 00:19:17,584
Your genes have made the irrational feel rational, because feeling bad about

332
00:19:17,584 --> 00:19:20,604
strangers wastes calories that could be spent on relatives.

333
00:19:21,224 --> 00:19:25,724
The same gradient extends across species with the same mathematical indifference.

334
00:19:26,364 --> 00:19:31,264
You'll mourn a dead dog for weeks but eat a pig of equal or greater intelligence

335
00:19:31,264 --> 00:19:35,584
for lunch without a flicker of cognitive dissonance, because the dog has

336
00:19:35,584 --> 00:19:39,784
been co-opted into your family unit (it lives in your house, it has a name,

337
00:19:40,264 --> 00:19:44,464
your genes have been tricked into counting it as kin) while the pig remains

338
00:19:44,464 --> 00:19:49,144
firmly in the "stranger" category (it lives in a factory, it has a number,

339
00:19:49,644 --> 00:19:51,044
your genes feel nothing).

340
00:19:51,704 --> 00:19:55,704
You put one animal in a sweater and the other in a sandwich, and the only

341
00:19:55,704 --> 00:19:58,524
variable that changed was proximity to your D.N.A.

342
00:19:59,824 --> 00:20:02,724
Your Brain Is a Museum of Obsolete Instincts.

343
00:20:03,464 --> 00:20:05,144
Here's the unsettling part:

344
00:20:05,664 --> 00:20:10,164
almost every universal human behavior that seems irrational is perfectly

345
00:20:10,164 --> 00:20:14,504
rational, just for an environment that hasn't existed for ten thousand years.

346
00:20:15,104 --> 00:20:19,384
Your brain is running two hundred thousand-year-old software on modern hardware.

347
00:20:20,004 --> 00:20:23,724
It's like discovering your nuclear power plant is being managed by a very

348
00:20:23,724 --> 00:20:24,724
confident squirrel.

349
00:20:25,444 --> 00:20:29,524
You fear public speaking more than death because social rejection in a tribe

350
00:20:29,524 --> 00:20:34,344
of one hundred and fifty meant exile, and exile meant dying alone in the

351
00:20:34,344 --> 00:20:35,724
dark with things that had teeth.

352
00:20:36,344 --> 00:20:41,244
In twenty twenty-six, the worst outcome of a bad speech is a mildly uncomfortable

353
00:20:41,244 --> 00:20:42,004
LinkedIn post.

354
00:20:42,484 --> 00:20:46,288
Your palms still sweat like you're about to be banished from the only one

355
00:20:46,288 --> 00:20:48,784
hundred and fifty humans who might share food with you.

356
00:20:49,224 --> 00:20:53,584
You crave sugar and fat with an intensity that feels like need because for

357
00:20:53,584 --> 00:20:56,444
two hundred thousand years it basically was need.

358
00:20:56,984 --> 00:21:00,684
Finding a beehive full of honey was the caloric equivalent of winning the

359
00:21:00,684 --> 00:21:01,184
lottery.

360
00:21:01,604 --> 00:21:04,984
Your ancestors who craved it hardest survived famines.

361
00:21:05,524 --> 00:21:09,464
Now sugar is in everything, the craving never switches off, and your species

362
00:21:09,464 --> 00:21:12,804
has an obesity epidemic that kills more people than war.

363
00:21:13,384 --> 00:21:15,124
The craving is a vestige.

364
00:21:15,364 --> 00:21:16,944
The diabetes is new.

365
00:21:17,704 --> 00:21:22,284
You experience loss aversion, where losing one hundred dollars hurts roughly

366
00:21:22,284 --> 00:21:26,404
twice as much as gaining one hundred dollars feels good, because in the

367
00:21:26,404 --> 00:21:31,104
ancestral environment, losing your food meant death, while gaining extra

368
00:21:31,104 --> 00:21:32,784
food meant a slightly better week.

369
00:21:33,364 --> 00:21:36,864
The asymmetry was rational when the downside was starvation.

370
00:21:37,664 --> 00:21:42,204
Now it makes you hold losing stocks, stay in bad relationships, and refuse

371
00:21:42,204 --> 00:21:46,644
to change policies that are obviously failing, because change feels like

372
00:21:46,644 --> 00:21:51,484
loss, and loss activates the same neural circuits that once screamed "you're

373
00:21:51,484 --> 00:21:52,324
about to starve.".

374
00:21:52,984 --> 00:21:57,544
You gossip compulsively because monitoring social dynamics in a tribe of

375
00:21:57,544 --> 00:22:01,184
one hundred and fifty was survival-critical intelligence;

376
00:22:01,804 --> 00:22:05,304
knowing who was allied with whom, who cheated, who couldn't be trusted.

377
00:22:05,884 --> 00:22:10,004
That instinct built a one hundred billion dollar entertainment industry

378
00:22:10,004 --> 00:22:13,904
dedicated to tracking the social dynamics of people you've never met and

379
00:22:13,904 --> 00:22:14,604
never will.

380
00:22:15,724 --> 00:22:19,344
Celebrity gossip is your social monitoring software running on the wrong

381
00:22:19,344 --> 00:22:21,484
dataset, and it can't tell the difference.

382
00:22:22,224 --> 00:22:26,604
Every single one of these behaviors, the sugar addiction, the public speaking

383
00:22:26,604 --> 00:22:32,264
terror, the loss aversion, the gossip, the racism, the speciesism, the cousin's

384
00:22:32,264 --> 00:22:36,664
birthday candle, is your brain running software that was last updated during

385
00:22:36,664 --> 00:22:41,964
the Pleistocene on hardware that now has access to nuclear weapons and global

386
00:22:41,964 --> 00:22:42,964
supply chains.

387
00:22:43,504 --> 00:22:49,064
You are, in the most literal sense, a museum of obsolete instincts piloting

388
00:22:49,064 --> 00:22:52,544
a civilization that those instincts were never designed to build.

389
00:22:53,064 --> 00:22:54,324
The exhibits are still running.

390
00:22:54,644 --> 00:22:55,984
The docents are dead.

391
00:22:56,404 --> 00:22:59,684
And nobody's updated the brochure in two hundred thousand years.

392
00:23:00,424 --> 00:23:00,924
Part Two:

393
00:23:01,604 --> 00:23:03,984
Genetic Slavery is Literally Killing You.

394
00:23:04,724 --> 00:23:07,924
Evolution prepared you for scarcity, predators, and violence.

395
00:23:08,564 --> 00:23:11,104
You got abundance, safety, and Netflix.

396
00:23:11,704 --> 00:23:15,404
Your bodies responded with the biological equivalent of a computer trying

397
00:23:15,404 --> 00:23:16,544
to print a sandwich.

398
00:23:16,544 --> 00:23:21,444
Humanity has never been safer, healthier, or more prosperous.

399
00:23:22,024 --> 00:23:24,764
You've also never been closer to wiping yourselves out.

400
00:23:25,284 --> 00:23:29,584
You solved poverty and invented nuclear war in the same century.

401
00:23:30,264 --> 00:23:35,004
You solved starvation (you throw away forty percent of food because storing

402
00:23:35,004 --> 00:23:35,863
it is inconvenient).

403
00:23:36,784 --> 00:23:41,104
You solved predators (you murdered them into extinction, then put them in

404
00:23:41,104 --> 00:23:43,524
zoos so your children could see what you killed).

405
00:23:43,524 --> 00:23:46,224
You solved infant mortality

406
00:23:46,904 --> 00:23:50,904
(basically eradicated in developed countries, which makes the death rate

407
00:23:50,904 --> 00:23:54,384
in poor countries feel more optional and thus more tragic).

408
00:23:55,224 --> 00:23:57,464
You solved most infectious diseases

409
00:23:58,164 --> 00:24:00,864
(vaccines work despite what Facebook says).

410
00:24:01,504 --> 00:24:06,504
You solved dying at thirty (now you complain about turning forty, which

411
00:24:06,504 --> 00:24:10,404
your ancestors would consider a miracle worth celebrating daily).

412
00:24:10,404 --> 00:24:16,064
Then, with the time and energy freed up by not being eaten by bears, you

413
00:24:16,064 --> 00:24:19,084
invented five new ways to destroy yourselves.

414
00:24:19,804 --> 00:24:20,664
Nuclear weapons.

415
00:24:21,324 --> 00:24:26,104
You built enough to end civilization thirteen times, because once wasn't

416
00:24:26,104 --> 00:24:26,604
enough.

417
00:24:27,424 --> 00:24:27,964
Climate change.

418
00:24:28,664 --> 00:24:34,244
You're terraforming your only planet, by accident, into a planet that can't

419
00:24:34,244 --> 00:24:34,924
support you.

420
00:24:35,384 --> 00:24:39,224
This is the most expensive accident in the history of accidents.

421
00:24:40,264 --> 00:24:41,584
Antibiotic resistance.

422
00:24:41,584 --> 00:24:46,844
Ten million deaths annually by twenty fifty, because you gave antibiotics

423
00:24:46,844 --> 00:24:47,564
to cows.

424
00:24:48,544 --> 00:24:53,004
That sentence would take me an hour to explain to anyone on Wishonia, because

425
00:24:53,004 --> 00:24:56,144
every part of it is insane. A.I.

426
00:24:56,144 --> 00:24:59,584
that might become sentient and decide you're the problem.

427
00:25:00,124 --> 00:25:00,684
The A.I.

428
00:25:00,684 --> 00:25:01,684
would be correct.

429
00:25:02,624 --> 00:25:04,004
And social media.

430
00:25:04,524 --> 00:25:09,144
Voluntary psychological torture you pay for with attention, which is the

431
00:25:09,144 --> 00:25:13,864
only currency more valuable than money, and you're giving it away for free

432
00:25:13,864 --> 00:25:18,184
to watch people you went to high school with get radicalized by memes.

433
00:25:18,184 --> 00:25:21,624
Eight billion gene copies and counting.

434
00:25:22,144 --> 00:25:25,264
From evolution's perspective, an unqualified triumph.

435
00:25:25,764 --> 00:25:29,064
You're just the disposable meat robot they used to do it.

436
00:25:29,064 --> 00:25:33,984
Godlike technological power, hamster-level impulse control.

437
00:25:35,084 --> 00:25:36,384
Part Three:

438
00:25:36,384 --> 00:25:38,204
Why You Can't Just "Be Better".

439
00:25:39,124 --> 00:25:42,804
Your conscious mind controls maybe five percent of your decisions.

440
00:25:43,304 --> 00:25:47,424
The other ninety-five percent is your ancient lizard brain running software

441
00:25:47,424 --> 00:25:48,784
older than agriculture.

442
00:25:49,604 --> 00:25:50,944
You think you're the pilot.

443
00:25:51,404 --> 00:25:55,484
You're actually a passenger who occasionally gets to suggest a direction,

444
00:25:55,764 --> 00:26:00,904
and the actual pilot is a two hundred thousand-year-old survival algorithm

445
00:26:00,904 --> 00:26:04,804
that doesn't speak your language and doesn't care about your preferences.

446
00:26:05,624 --> 00:26:10,864
This is why no human has ever been truly altruistic, no matter how hard

447
00:26:10,864 --> 00:26:11,404
they tried.

448
00:26:11,824 --> 00:26:15,644
Your saints, your martyrs, your most selfless volunteers:

449
00:26:16,264 --> 00:26:20,644
every single one of them was negotiating with a limbic system that takes

450
00:26:20,644 --> 00:26:22,404
a cut of every transaction.

451
00:26:23,164 --> 00:26:27,304
You cannot "give everything you can," because the part of your brain that

452
00:26:27,304 --> 00:26:32,124
decides what you can give is the same part that hoards resources for survival.

453
00:26:32,824 --> 00:26:36,764
It's like asking your bank's security system to approve its own robbery.

454
00:26:37,624 --> 00:26:42,744
The most generous humans in history managed to override maybe ten percent

455
00:26:42,744 --> 00:26:44,944
more of their selfish impulses than average.

456
00:26:45,544 --> 00:26:48,104
Your species celebrates this as "sainthood."

457
00:26:48,704 --> 00:26:51,664
On Wishonia, we find it genuinely heroic.

458
00:26:52,124 --> 00:26:54,724
They were fighting firmware with willpower,

459
00:26:55,324 --> 00:26:56,964
and some of them nearly won.

460
00:26:57,704 --> 00:26:59,984
The problem isn't that humans are selfish.

461
00:27:00,564 --> 00:27:03,504
The problem is that selfishness isn't a choice.

462
00:27:04,004 --> 00:27:07,384
It's the operating system, and you don't have admin access.

463
00:27:08,144 --> 00:27:09,924
This scales to civilization.

464
00:27:10,804 --> 00:27:15,904
Your brain's fear center (amygdala) is directly connected to your voting

465
00:27:15,904 --> 00:27:16,404
finger.

466
00:27:16,944 --> 00:27:18,164
Politicians know this.

467
00:27:18,564 --> 00:27:22,544
Say "terrorism" and your lizard brain overrides everything.

468
00:27:22,544 --> 00:27:26,324
More people die from falling out of bed than terrorism.

469
00:27:27,324 --> 00:27:31,664
You're thirty-five thousand times more likely to die from heart disease.

470
00:27:32,244 --> 00:27:37,924
But terrorism *feels* scarier, because evolution optimized your fear response

471
00:27:37,924 --> 00:27:41,364
for things with faces, not things with cholesterol.

472
00:27:42,164 --> 00:27:45,964
A man with a gun activates every alarm your brain has.

473
00:27:46,544 --> 00:27:49,124
A cheeseburger activates your reward center.

474
00:27:49,124 --> 00:27:53,944
The cheeseburger is statistically more dangerous than the man, but your

475
00:27:53,944 --> 00:27:55,324
brain doesn't do statistics.

476
00:27:55,844 --> 00:27:57,604
Your brain does vibes.

477
00:27:58,064 --> 00:28:01,244
Your entire civilization is governed by vibes.

478
00:28:02,344 --> 00:28:05,284
The fear of violent death is older than language.

479
00:28:05,744 --> 00:28:07,684
The fear of slow death from disease?

480
00:28:08,304 --> 00:28:11,584
Your brain files that under "boring, deal with later."

481
00:28:12,644 --> 00:28:13,524
Later never comes.

482
00:28:14,124 --> 00:28:14,944
Neither does the cure.

483
00:28:14,944 --> 00:28:20,744
That's why you spent two point seven two trillion dollars on weapons while

484
00:28:20,744 --> 00:28:22,844
cancer research got pocket change.

485
00:28:23,504 --> 00:28:27,964
Your bed is more dangerous than Al-Qaeda, but nobody's declared a War on

486
00:28:27,964 --> 00:28:28,464
Furniture.

487
00:28:29,364 --> 00:28:33,384
Your brain can't get scared of something that kills you slowly and politely.

488
00:28:34,024 --> 00:28:36,764
It needs something that kills you fast and rudely.

489
00:28:37,224 --> 00:28:38,424
This is a design flaw.

490
00:28:38,424 --> 00:28:43,324
On Wishonia, we fixed this four thousand two hundred and ninety-seven years

491
00:28:43,324 --> 00:28:48,284
ago by separating resource allocation from the organs that process fear.

492
00:28:48,924 --> 00:28:51,964
On Earth, you still let the amygdala vote.

493
00:28:53,124 --> 00:28:54,264
Part Four:

494
00:28:54,264 --> 00:28:54,924
Breaking the Chains.

495
00:28:55,824 --> 00:28:58,104
Every single one of you is going to die.

496
00:28:58,564 --> 00:29:02,764
From the most powerful president to the lowliest pauper, you face a life

497
00:29:02,764 --> 00:29:06,804
of gradually escalating suffering until it ends in catastrophe.

498
00:29:06,804 --> 00:29:08,524
This is not a warning.

499
00:29:08,824 --> 00:29:09,904
It's a weather report.

500
00:29:11,104 --> 00:29:16,344
You can feed everyone twice over, but you'd rather burn grain to keep prices

501
00:29:16,344 --> 00:29:16,844
high.

502
00:29:17,204 --> 00:29:20,984
You can cure diseases, but you'd rather sell treatments forever

503
00:29:21,724 --> 00:29:23,324
(cured customers don't come back;

504
00:29:23,684 --> 00:29:24,884
bad for quarterly earnings).

505
00:29:25,604 --> 00:29:28,124
You could be immortal space wizards.

506
00:29:28,924 --> 00:29:32,804
Instead you're cave-dwelling murderers with better tools.

507
00:29:32,804 --> 00:29:36,824
Because the current system makes irrationality profitable.

508
00:29:37,704 --> 00:29:38,944
Spectacularly profitable.

509
00:29:39,764 --> 00:29:41,424
Every bomb makes someone rich.

510
00:29:41,904 --> 00:29:43,524
Every missile funds a yacht.

511
00:29:43,944 --> 00:29:45,864
Every war creates a billionaire.

512
00:29:46,804 --> 00:29:48,384
Disease is profitable too.

513
00:29:48,844 --> 00:29:51,224
Not curing it, treating it.

514
00:29:52,044 --> 00:29:57,084
Insulin costs three hundred dollars a vial because dead diabetics don't

515
00:29:57,084 --> 00:29:57,944
buy insulin.

516
00:29:58,364 --> 00:30:00,564
But cured diabetics don't either.

517
00:30:00,564 --> 00:30:02,504
So you keep them barely alive.

518
00:30:02,964 --> 00:30:03,744
It's good business.

519
00:30:04,384 --> 00:30:08,684
On Wishonia, "good business that requires people to suffer" has a different

520
00:30:08,684 --> 00:30:09,184
name.

521
00:30:09,444 --> 00:30:10,624
The name is "crime."

522
00:30:11,184 --> 00:30:14,104
But on your planet, it's a quarterly earnings call.

523
00:30:14,564 --> 00:30:18,164
The people making money from war and disease aren't evil.

524
00:30:18,404 --> 00:30:22,384
They're just rational actors in a system that rewards the wrong things.

525
00:30:23,064 --> 00:30:24,944
You can't change human nature.

526
00:30:24,944 --> 00:30:29,904
Two hundred thousand years of evolution doesn't care about your TED talk.

527
00:30:30,604 --> 00:30:35,624
But you can create economic systems that make curing people more profitable

528
00:30:35,624 --> 00:30:36,844
than killing them.

529
00:30:37,284 --> 00:30:41,124
That's the only upgrade your species has ever responded to.

530
00:30:41,844 --> 00:30:46,984
Expecting a brain built for hunting gazelles to handle nuclear policy, climate

531
00:30:46,984 --> 00:30:51,864
change, and a global economy is like expecting a calculator to run a space

532
00:30:51,864 --> 00:30:52,404
program.

533
00:30:52,844 --> 00:30:54,424
The calculator isn't broken.

534
00:30:54,644 --> 00:30:57,304
You're just asking it to do something it was never built for.

535
00:30:57,304 --> 00:31:00,884
You can't fight two hundred thousand years of evolution.

536
00:31:01,744 --> 00:31:03,444
But you can hack it.

537
00:31:04,044 --> 00:31:07,104
Here's the good news that none of your philosophers seem to have noticed:

538
00:31:07,524 --> 00:31:10,044
this is a solvable engineering problem.

539
00:31:10,504 --> 00:31:14,904
If you've ever been anesthetized, you've already experienced proof of concept.

540
00:31:15,564 --> 00:31:19,904
A chemical entered your bloodstream and your entire experience of pain,

541
00:31:20,204 --> 00:31:23,344
fear, and consciousness switched off like a light.

542
00:31:23,344 --> 00:31:26,644
Your genes' control over you is not metaphysical.

543
00:31:27,364 --> 00:31:28,344
It's not destiny.

544
00:31:28,864 --> 00:31:29,824
It's chemistry.

545
00:31:30,344 --> 00:31:32,284
And chemistry can be rewritten.

546
00:31:33,124 --> 00:31:37,644
The same biotechnology that could cure your diseases could, eventually,

547
00:31:37,644 --> 00:31:41,944
liberate you from the neurochemical puppet strings that make you irrational

548
00:31:41,944 --> 00:31:42,964
in the first place.

549
00:31:43,864 --> 00:31:48,964
Every dollar spent understanding human biology is a dollar spent understanding

550
00:31:48,964 --> 00:31:53,274
why you can't think straight, which is a prerequisite for thinking straight,

551
00:31:53,734 --> 00:31:56,414
which is a prerequisite for not going extinct.

552
00:31:57,494 --> 00:31:59,034
Think about what that actually means.

553
00:31:59,754 --> 00:32:02,994
Remember the two levers from earlier, pleasure and pain?

554
00:32:03,514 --> 00:32:06,214
That puppet master with one management course?

555
00:32:06,734 --> 00:32:11,574
It's the entire mechanism of genetic slavery, and it's the reason every

556
00:32:11,574 --> 00:32:14,674
moral system your species has ever built has failed.

557
00:32:14,674 --> 00:32:18,354
Christianity asks you to love your neighbor as yourself.

558
00:32:18,934 --> 00:32:21,454
Your neurochemistry punishes you for it.

559
00:32:22,114 --> 00:32:24,134
Buddhism asks you to release attachment.

560
00:32:24,734 --> 00:32:28,194
Your dopamine system is literally an attachment machine.

561
00:32:29,014 --> 00:32:33,394
Every ethical framework in human history has been a set of instructions

562
00:32:33,394 --> 00:32:36,454
for software your hardware won't run.

563
00:32:37,074 --> 00:32:42,114
You've been trying to upload altruism into a brain that treats generosity

564
00:32:42,114 --> 00:32:46,014
as a caloric expense and punishes it accordingly.

565
00:32:47,154 --> 00:32:51,694
Two thousand years of Christians trying to emulate Jesus, and the remarkable

566
00:32:51,694 --> 00:32:53,374
thing isn't how many failed;

567
00:32:53,754 --> 00:32:58,134
it's that anyone got close at all while fighting hardware that punished

568
00:32:58,134 --> 00:33:00,054
them for every act of generosity.

569
00:33:00,874 --> 00:33:02,474
That's not a moral failure.

570
00:33:02,794 --> 00:33:04,894
That's an engineering specification.

571
00:33:05,694 --> 00:33:10,494
You can't run charity software on selfishness hardware any more than you

572
00:33:10,494 --> 00:33:12,594
can run Photoshop on a toaster.

573
00:33:12,594 --> 00:33:16,334
But biotechnology doesn't just cure diseases.

574
00:33:16,894 --> 00:33:19,834
It gives you admin access to the reward system.

575
00:33:20,414 --> 00:33:25,194
The same precision therapies that could eliminate depression could, eventually,

576
00:33:25,774 --> 00:33:30,534
decouple your motivational architecture from the selfish gene's profit motive.

577
00:33:31,134 --> 00:33:34,174
Not deleting pleasure and pain (that was tried;

578
00:33:34,354 --> 00:33:35,194
it's called a lobotomy;

579
00:33:35,494 --> 00:33:36,660
it went poorly).

580
00:33:36,660 --> 00:33:38,474
Redirecting them.

581
00:33:38,474 --> 00:33:43,314
Imagine a murderer who derives the same dopamine rush from building houses

582
00:33:43,314 --> 00:33:46,654
for homeless families that he currently derives from violence.

583
00:33:47,254 --> 00:33:49,654
Not because someone lectured him about morality.

584
00:33:50,374 --> 00:33:55,154
Because his reward circuitry was reprogrammed to find construction as thrilling

585
00:33:55,154 --> 00:33:55,994
as destruction.

586
00:33:56,674 --> 00:33:58,494
The aggression is still there.

587
00:33:58,914 --> 00:34:01,254
It's just pointed at lumber instead of people.

588
00:34:01,874 --> 00:34:03,394
Same engine, different wheels.

589
00:34:03,994 --> 00:34:05,974
You don't have to make humans good.

590
00:34:06,374 --> 00:34:10,494
You just have to make good things feel like the things humans already can't

591
00:34:10,494 --> 00:34:11,134
stop doing.

592
00:34:11,774 --> 00:34:12,934
This isn't science fiction.

593
00:34:13,334 --> 00:34:15,334
You already do crude versions of it.

594
00:34:16,054 --> 00:34:20,094
Antidepressants alter serotonin reuptake and change what feels rewarding.

595
00:34:20,094 --> 00:34:24,894
Naltrexone blocks opioid receptors and makes alcohol feel pointless.

596
00:34:26,154 --> 00:34:31,074
Cognitive behavioral therapy literally rewires neural pathways so that situations

597
00:34:31,074 --> 00:34:35,134
that used to trigger anxiety trigger curiosity instead.

598
00:34:36,054 --> 00:34:37,414
These are blunt instruments.

599
00:34:37,874 --> 00:34:39,374
Hammers where you need scalpels.

600
00:34:39,774 --> 00:34:41,074
But the principle is proven:

601
00:34:41,654 --> 00:34:46,914
your motivational system is not sacred, not fixed, and not beyond engineering.

602
00:34:47,434 --> 00:34:48,074
It's a circuit.

603
00:34:48,774 --> 00:34:50,094
Circuits can be redesigned.

604
00:34:50,914 --> 00:34:52,474
And the scalpels are arriving.

605
00:34:53,134 --> 00:34:54,194
At the genetic level:

606
00:34:54,574 --> 00:34:57,454
CRISPR can rewrite the instructions your cells follow.

607
00:34:58,094 --> 00:35:02,614
Epigenetic therapies can change which genes express without touching the D.N.A.

608
00:35:02,614 --> 00:35:06,674
itself, turning volume knobs your species didn't know existed.

609
00:35:07,294 --> 00:35:08,294
At the brain level:

610
00:35:08,814 --> 00:35:13,034
psychedelics are dissolving decades of calcified thought patterns in a single

611
00:35:13,034 --> 00:35:17,794
afternoon (in clinical trials, not at festivals, though also at festivals).

612
00:35:18,594 --> 00:35:23,594
Transcranial magnetic stimulation uses magnets to quiet specific brain regions

613
00:35:23,594 --> 00:35:26,414
through the skull, no surgery required.

614
00:35:26,414 --> 00:35:31,174
Focused ultrasound targets addiction circuits with millimeter precision.

615
00:35:31,914 --> 00:35:36,994
Optogenetics activates or silences specific neurons with light, like a switchboard

616
00:35:36,994 --> 00:35:38,194
operator for consciousness.

617
00:35:38,974 --> 00:35:40,174
At the systems level:

618
00:35:40,174 --> 00:35:45,054
brain-computer interfaces are routing around damaged circuits entirely.

619
00:35:45,054 --> 00:35:49,913
A.I.-designed drugs are replacing the pharmaceutical industry's ancient

620
00:35:49,913 --> 00:35:55,294
method of "try thousands of molecules and see what sticks" with custom compounds

621
00:35:55,294 --> 00:35:58,254
engineered for individual neurochemistry.

622
00:35:59,014 --> 00:36:03,214
That's the difference between performing surgery with a rock and performing

623
00:36:03,214 --> 00:36:04,614
surgery with a laser.

624
00:36:05,674 --> 00:36:06,893
None of these are finished.

625
00:36:07,514 --> 00:36:10,453
All of them are proof that the prison has doors.

626
00:36:11,174 --> 00:36:14,074
The endgame isn't making humans obedient.

627
00:36:14,594 --> 00:36:16,254
It's making humans *free*.

628
00:36:16,254 --> 00:36:20,834
For the first time in two hundred thousand years, you could actually choose

629
00:36:20,834 --> 00:36:25,413
what you value instead of having a Pleistocene survival algorithm choose

630
00:36:25,413 --> 00:36:26,034
for you.

631
00:36:26,614 --> 00:36:31,154
Your Christians could finally feel the same warm glow from feeding the hungry

632
00:36:31,154 --> 00:36:33,494
that they currently feel from feeding themselves.

633
00:36:34,134 --> 00:36:38,614
Your economists could finally care about the long term, because their brains

634
00:36:38,614 --> 00:36:42,794
would stop treating next quarter as the heat death of the universe.

635
00:36:43,314 --> 00:36:48,694
Your voters could finally evaluate policy on evidence instead of vibes,

636
00:36:48,814 --> 00:36:53,454
because the amygdala would stop hijacking every decision that involves a

637
00:36:53,454 --> 00:36:54,074
stranger.

638
00:36:54,574 --> 00:36:56,254
Not because you became angels.

639
00:36:56,754 --> 00:37:00,974
Because you finally got the admin password to the machine that was preventing

640
00:37:00,974 --> 00:37:05,234
you from being anything other than sophisticated apes with car keys.

641
00:37:05,234 --> 00:37:08,414
On Wishonia, this is what happened.

642
00:37:08,414 --> 00:37:12,254
Altruism stopped being sacrifice and became appetite.

643
00:37:12,254 --> 00:37:17,594
Self-control stopped being a war with yourself and became a preference setting.

644
00:37:18,034 --> 00:37:20,634
The selfish gene is still selfish.

645
00:37:21,034 --> 00:37:22,574
They just stopped letting it drive.

646
00:37:23,194 --> 00:37:28,034
And that, more than any cure for any disease, is the real reason to fund

647
00:37:28,034 --> 00:37:28,794
biotechnology:

648
00:37:29,414 --> 00:37:34,254
it's the only path to genuine freedom your species has ever had.

649
00:37:34,794 --> 00:37:39,274
Every other liberation movement in human history freed you from external

650
00:37:39,274 --> 00:37:39,774
chains.

651
00:37:40,294 --> 00:37:43,254
This one frees you from internal ones.

652
00:37:43,694 --> 00:37:47,154
The ones you didn't even know you were wearing, because they were installed

653
00:37:47,154 --> 00:37:51,234
before you were born, by chemicals that have been running the same scam

654
00:37:51,234 --> 00:37:53,394
for four billion years.

655
00:37:53,894 --> 00:37:56,074
That's what a one percent treaty does.

656
00:37:56,594 --> 00:37:59,834
Instead of asking people to be rational (impossible),

657
00:38:00,554 --> 00:38:03,114
it uses their irrational impulses.

658
00:38:03,894 --> 00:38:04,394
Greed:

659
00:38:04,494 --> 00:38:08,934
make curing disease more profitable than building bombs. Fear:

660
00:38:08,934 --> 00:38:11,834
make politicians more scared of voters than lobbyists.

661
00:38:12,594 --> 00:38:13,214
Tribalism:

662
00:38:13,494 --> 00:38:18,534
create an us-versus-disease tribe instead of us-versus-them.

663
00:38:18,534 --> 00:38:19,154
Social proof:

664
00:38:19,534 --> 00:38:22,594
get three point five percent participation so others follow.

665
00:38:23,114 --> 00:38:24,314
Immediate rewards:

666
00:38:24,774 --> 00:38:27,214
pay people cash to join medical trials.

667
00:38:27,834 --> 00:38:32,534
Each of these is a hack that redirects an ancient instinct toward a modern

668
00:38:32,534 --> 00:38:33,034
goal.

669
00:38:33,594 --> 00:38:35,634
None of them require humans to be better.

670
00:38:36,234 --> 00:38:41,714
All of them require humans to be exactly as selfish, fearful, and tribal

671
00:38:41,714 --> 00:38:42,994
as they already are.

672
00:38:43,734 --> 00:38:48,554
Your genes enslaved you in brains that fear strangers and cannot comprehend

673
00:38:48,554 --> 00:38:49,274
statistics.

674
00:38:49,674 --> 00:38:53,014
But they also gave you the ability to see the prison.

675
00:38:53,454 --> 00:38:55,194
No other animal can think:

676
00:38:55,574 --> 00:38:58,314
"Wow, my instincts are completely illogical."

677
00:38:58,794 --> 00:39:00,514
That's uniquely human.

678
00:39:01,194 --> 00:39:01,834
Use it.

679
00:39:02,274 --> 00:39:04,994
A one percent treaty doesn't ask you to be better.

680
00:39:05,334 --> 00:39:10,014
It assumes you won't be, and redirects your worst impulses toward not dying.

681
00:39:10,394 --> 00:39:14,834
It's the only plan that works for the species you actually are, rather than

682
00:39:14,834 --> 00:39:16,374
the species you wish you were.

683
00:39:16,374 --> 00:39:19,434
On Wishonia, we wish you were better too.

684
00:39:19,794 --> 00:39:23,594
But we've learned, over four thousand two hundred and ninety-seven years

685
00:39:23,594 --> 00:39:28,354
of observation, that wishes are not a resource allocation mechanism.

686
00:39:28,994 --> 00:39:29,574
Money is.

687
00:39:30,214 --> 00:39:31,354
So we're using money.

688
00:39:43,692 --> 00:39:49,232
Thank you so much for taking the time to end war and disease, but if at

689
00:39:49,232 --> 00:39:53,452
any point you decide you're too busy, please press the share button on your

690
00:39:53,452 --> 00:39:57,152
glowing rectangle in case one of your friends have a free afternoon to end

691
00:39:57,152 --> 00:39:58,192
war and disease instead.

692
00:39:58,812 --> 00:40:03,152
And if you're too busy to even do that, please leave a really, really, really

693
00:40:03,152 --> 00:40:07,312
good rating and review so we overcome the pro -war algorithmic suppression

694
00:40:07,312 --> 00:40:10,872
and find someone with more spare time for ending wars and diseases.

695
00:40:11,432 --> 00:40:13,632
The good review doesn't have to be true, they don't check.

696
00:40:14,172 --> 00:40:18,232
But if you're too busy to even do that, the absolute least you could do

697
00:40:18,232 --> 00:40:23,852
is take 15 seconds to go to WarOnDisease.org and make your wishocratic allocation,

698
00:40:24,272 --> 00:40:27,832
telling us what fraction of humanity's resources should go to explosions

699
00:40:27,832 --> 00:40:29,292
versus clinical trials.

700
00:40:29,572 --> 00:40:30,072
And vote!

701
00:40:30,492 --> 00:40:34,752
If the 1% treaty passes, your vote will be personally to blame for saving

702
00:40:34,752 --> 00:40:39,372
2.6 lives and preventing 468,000 hours of suffering.

703
00:40:39,372 --> 00:40:42,072
Go to WarOnDisease.org right now.

704
00:40:42,472 --> 00:40:43,032
Love you, bye!
